    "content": "> [!warning] Scaffolding Removal in Part VI\n> All external scaffolding is removed in Part VI. You are alone with the Blank Sheet.\n\n\n---\n\n## Part V Mastery Gate\n\nDemonstrate:\n\n- ability to preserve premise under revision\n- ability to diagnose stakeholder feedback\n- ability to re-brief rather than endlessly patch\n- ability to defend decisions without hiding behind AI\n- ability to refuse when necessary\n- ability to adapt your directorial approach to an unfamiliar constraint\n- **ability to define scope and revision discipline**\n- **ability to record the human contribution explicitly in a professional context**\n- **(when collaborating) ability to agree economics and authorship before starting**\n\n> [!question] The Gate Question\n> Can you sit across from someone who cares about the outcome — a stakeholder, a client, a collaborator — and make a decision you can defend, even if they disagree? If you can only make decisions when no one is watching, you have not yet developed direction. If you can make decisions while someone watches, and explain them without defensiveness or capitulation, you have.\n\n---"
