    "content": "> [!important] Exit Criteria\n> You have passed when you can be dropped into an unfamiliar medium or domain and immediately structure the problem, build the pipeline, and defend the work.\n\n\n---\n\n## Part VI Mastery Gate\n\nDo not complete the intensive until you can:\n\n- originate a meaningful problem\n- formulate a premise without a prompt\n- construct a brief without a template\n- choose an appropriate production method\n- diagnose without a visible ladder\n- revise criteria when reality contradicts assumptions\n- defend a refusal\n- explain what the work is for\n- demonstrate an emerging position through actual work\n- solve an unfamiliar creative problem without course scaffolding\n- **synthesise visual and writing into one authored object when required**\n- **decide what of your process is public work**\n- **situate yourself honestly in relation to the problem you pursued**\n\n> [!warning] If the Blank-Sheet Test Is Weak, You Are Not \"Done\" Merely Because the Portfolios Are Polished.\n\n> [!question] The Gate Question\n> Can you look at the work you have made over twelve weeks and say, honestly, \"This is mine\"? Not \"I made this,\" but \"I chose this, I found this problem, I built this process, I can defend this decision, and I can take responsibility for what it does.\" If the answer is yes, you have completed the intensive. If the answer is \"mostly,\" you have identified what needs more practice. If the answer is no, you have identified what the next twelve weeks are for.\n\n---"
